42e2a223f","type":"text_block","style":{},"content":{"text":"(Kate/CEO) as a shadow admin** — i.e. an external EC mentor given broad, all-stage oversight of the Foundation workspace + the TVSF proposal so he can watch the pipeline and coach the team."},"history":[{"action":"created","actor_id":"system:import","timestamp":"2026-08-10T13:20:08.196Z","actor_name":"Document Import"}],"provenance":{"source":"imported","drafted_at":"2026-08-10T13:20:08.196Z","drafted_by":"system:import"},"library_eligible":true},{"id":"7ea1f7d0-b928-468b-85f3-0b4dc5036340","type":"bulleted_list","style":{},"content":{"items":[{"text":"Password (demo): `DemoPass123!` (same as the founders).","indent_level":0}]},"history":[{"action":"created","actor_id":"system:import","timestamp":"2026-08-10T13:20:08.196Z","actor_name":"Document Import"}],"provenance":{"source":"imported","drafted_at":"2026-08-10T13:20:08.196Z","drafted_by":"system:import"},"library_eligible":true},{"id":"17594824-ab39-4b7a-8be6-73f01fc57720","type":"heading","style":{},"content":{"text":"4. Deck facts (raw, for the library atoms)","level":2},"history":[{"action":"created","actor_id":"system:import","timestamp":"2026-08-10T13:20:08.196Z","actor_name":"Document Import"}],"provenance":{"source":"imported","drafted_at":"2026-08-10T13:20:08.196Z","drafted_by":"system:import"},"library_eligible":true},{"id":"8418ea21-173a-4f0d-b9dc-723991b3d7f0","type":"bulleted_list","style":{},"content":{"items":[{"text":"**Formwork economics (slide 4):** Traditional labor 336 hrs → 25 hrs; labor cost $11,588–$14,826 →","indent_level":0}]},"history":[{"action":"created","actor_id":"system:import","timestamp":"2026-08-10T13:20:08.196Z","actor_name":"Document Import"}],"provenance":{"source":"imported","drafted_at":"2026-08-10T13:20:08.196Z","drafted_by":"system:import"},"library_eligible":true},{"id":"505b76b8-486d-4fee-82a5-3e1ace14cce8","type":"text_block","style":{},"content":{"text":"$2,549 (set crew); material $8,499–$10,561 (15% waste) → $8,074–$10,033 (5% waste). Total savings ~47% of cost, ~11 days. Basis: 2,100 sq ft single-family home, Ohio."},"history":[{"action":"created","actor_id":"system:import","timestamp":"2026-08-10T13:20:08.196Z","actor_name":"Document Import"}],"provenance":{"source":"imported","drafted_at":"2026-08-10T13:20:08.196Z","drafted_by":"system:import"},"library_eligible":true},{"id":"3d2568a1-b66f-4c1b-8249-cd1c5df753cf","type":"bulleted_list","style":{},"content":{"items":[{"text":"**Technology (slides 6, 8):** plans downloaded to the printer; concrete pumped into the machine;","indent_level":0}]},"history":[{"action":"created","actor_id":"system:import","timestamp":"2026-08-10T13:20:08.196Z","actor_name":"Document Import"}],"provenance":{"source":"imported","drafted_at":"2026-08-10T13:20:08.196Z","drafted_by":"system:import"},"library_eligible":true},{"id":"18be1814-06b0-4215-989e-23e6447744e2","type":"text_block","style":{},"content":{"text":"lays concrete one layer at a time; printing trolley moves laterally + vertically; whole machine travels along runway rails; electrically powered. Uses **common local concrete, not proprietary mortar**; an **external gate controls flow at the nozzle**. Prints wall shape directly, eliminating the build-strip-repair-clean cycle; saves ~311 labor hrs/home; cuts production cost ~47–50%; cuts material cost ~60–65% vs mortar-based printers."},"history":[{"action":"created","actor_id":"system:import","timestamp":"2026-08-10T13:20:08.196Z","actor_name":"Document Import"}],"provenance":{"source":"imported","drafted_at":"2026-08-10T13:20:08.196Z","drafted_by":"system:import"},"library_eligible":true},{"id":"07e57ebe-9203-4c2d-89c3-10bc9f3e0427","type":"bulleted_list","style":{},"content":{"items":[{"text":"**Market (slide 5):** TAM **$410B** (2026 housing market); SAM **$23.7B** (formwork in single-family","indent_level":0}]},"history":[{"action":"created","actor_id":"system:import","timestamp":"2026-08-10T13:20:08.196Z","actor_name":"Document Import"}],"provenance":{"source":"imported","drafted_at":"2026-08-10T13:20:08.196Z","drafted_by":"system:import"},"library_eligible":true},{"id":"de95fbad-e543-47db-81bb-b20f4685db55","type":"text_block","style":{},"content":{"text":"new builds); SOM **$27.4M**. 500,000 home supply/demand gap; 6% mortgage \"lock-in\"; new-build \"buy-down\" strategy; foundation 3D printing reduces overall home cost ~4%."},"history":[{"action":"created","actor_id":"system:import","timestamp":"2026-08-10T13:20:08.196Z","actor_name":"Document Import"}],"provenance":{"source":"imported","drafted_at":"2026-08-10T13:20:08.196Z","drafted_by":"system:import"},"library_eligible":true},{"id":"77988e59-b7c3-4565-8133-39271259cdd5","type":"bulleted_list","style":{},"content":{"items":[{"text":"**Competitive (slide 7):** vs Traditional Formwork, Vitruvian, COBOD International across Time,","indent_level":0}]},"history":[{"action":"created","actor_id":"system:import","timestamp":"2026-08-10T13:20:08.196Z","actor_name":"Document Import"}],"provenance":{"source":"imported","drafted_at":"2026-08-10T13:20:08.196Z","drafted_by":"system:import"},"library_eligible":true},{"id":"fa6eea7e-0a99-4e7e-b9cd-6a36c24a9a46","type":"text_block","style":{},"content":{"text":"Deployment, Material Accessibility, Project Costs, Scalability, Repeatable Workflow."},"history":[{"action":"created","actor_id":"system:import","timestamp":"2026-08-10T13:20:08.196Z","actor_name":"Document Import"}],"provenance":{"source":"imported","drafted_at":"2026-08-10T13:20:08.196Z","drafted_by":"system:import"},"library_eligible":true},{"id":"1df897d9-e129-4693-94aa-ce22f630b677","type":"bulleted_list","style":{},"content":{"items":[{"text":"**Dev stage (slide 9):** TRL 6–7. Customer requirements: rapid deployment, reduced labor,","indent_level":0}]},"history":[{"action":"created","actor_id":"system:import","timestamp":"2026-08-10T13:20:08.196Z","actor_name":"Document Import"}],"provenance":{"source":"imported","drafted_at":"2026-08-10T13:20:08.196Z","drafted_by":"system:import"},"library_eligible":true},{"id":"b54b44da-eb2b-42ff-8cfc-4a74e3f37c47","type":"text_block","style":{},"content":{"text":"structural reliability, locally sourced materials."},"history":[{"action":"created","actor_id":"system:import","timestamp":"2026-08-10T13:20:08.196Z","actor_name":"Document Import"}],"provenance":{"source":"imported","drafted_at":"2026-08-10T13:20:08.196Z","drafted_by":"system:import"},"library_eligible":true},{"id":"6eec1669-43d1-4724-9051-d58aaf70b6e7","type":"bulleted_list","style":{},"content":{"items":[{"text":"**Timeline (slide 10):** 14-month Gantt — Grants+Funding, Product R&D, Beta Prototype, Design","indent_level":0}]},"history":[{"action":"created","actor_id":"system:import","timestamp":"2026-08-10T13:20:08.196Z","actor_name":"Document Import"}],"provenance":{"source":"imported","drafted_at":"2026-08-10T13:20:08.196Z","drafted_by":"system:import"},"library_eligible":true},{"id":"b4fb4061-dd42-4835-a1c3-48d8208a1d08","type":"text_block","style":{},"content":{"text":"Finalization, Third-Party Performance Validation, First Printer Build."},"history":[{"action":"created","actor_id":"system:import","timestamp":"2026-08-10T13:20:08.196Z","actor_name":"Document Import"}],"provenance":{"source":"imported","drafted_at":"2026-08-10T13:20:08.196Z","drafted_by":"system:import"},"library_eligible":true},{"id":"f51ef562-94d2-4ce3-91be-293910ccffcb","type":"bulleted_list","style":{},"content":{"items":[{"text":"**Commercialization (slide 11):** proof-based adoption; local fragmented buyers; barriers trust/","indent_level":0}]},"history":[{"action":"created","actor_id":"system:import","timestamp":"2026-08-10T13:20:08.196Z","actor_name":"Document Import"}],"provenance":{"source":"imported","drafted_at":"2026-08-10T13:20:08.196Z","drafted_by":"system:import"},"library_eligible":true},{"id":"4a3fcc1b-b08c-4ce9-8656-d8beb1410bc2","type":"text_block","style":{},"content":{"text":"portability/cost; fits subcontractor workflow. Entry via TVSF + SBIR Phase I; sell to GCs/developers; \"printing as a service\"; partner with local schools + builders; demos/tours → pilot → repeat jobs."},"history":[{"action":"created","actor_id":"system:import","timestamp":"2026-08-10T13:20:08.196Z","actor_name":"Document Import"}],"provenance":{"source":"imported","drafted_at":"2026-08-10T13:20:08.196Z","drafted_by":"system:import"},"library_eligible":true},{"id":"f378b30e-be46-46f3-a580-cef934f3bee6","type":"bulleted_list","style":{},"content":{"items":[{"text":"**IP (slide 12):** U.S. Patent **11,273,574** (Scalable Three-Dimensional Printing Apparatus);","indent_level":0}]},"history":[{"action":"created","actor_id":"system:import","timestamp":"2026-08-10T13:20:08.196Z","actor_name":"Document Import"}],"provenance":{"source":"imported","drafted_at":"2026-08-10T13:20:08.196Z","drafted_by":"system:import"},"library_eligible":true},{"id":"527945d8-2a53-4a53-a583-49e2d2b2bbfa","type":"text_block","style":{},"content":{"text":"U.S. Patent **10,307,959 B2** (Concrete Delivery System)."},"history":[{"action":"created","actor_id":"system:import","timestamp":"2026-08-10T13:20:08.196Z","actor_name":"Document Import"}],"provenance":{"source":"imported","drafted_at":"2026-08-10T13:20:08.196Z","drafted_by":"system:import"},"library_eligible":true},{"id":"5a630bb2-ed61-4723-8c28-9e80260200a4","type":"bulleted_list","style":{},"content":{"items":[{"text":"**Business model (slide 13):** form a JV; program + prepare the print; **charge per cubic yard of","indent_level":0}]},"history":[{"action":"created","actor_id":"system:import","timestamp":"2026-08-10T13:20:08.197Z","actor_name":"Document Import"}],"provenance":{"source":"imported","drafted_at":"2026-08-10T13:20:08.196Z","drafted_by":"system:import"},"library_eligible":true},{"id":"524433e0-08f5-4b02-91b5-ea21f9f8fbf0","type":"text_block","style":{},"content":{"text":"concrete**; ≈$20,000 total price per job; contribution margin ≈**37.5%**."},"history":[{"action":"created","actor_id":"system:import","timestamp":"2026-08-10T13:20:08.197Z","actor_name":"Document Import"}],"provenance":{"source":"imported","drafted_at":"2026-08-10T13:20:08.197Z","drafted_by":"system:import"},"library_eligible":true},{"id":"0f3fae85-a558-478a-afc4-60c17b89cc61","type":"bulleted_list","style":{},"content":{"items":[{"text":"**Financials (slide 15):** fundraising $200k TVSF + $150k SBIR + $1.8M+ equity; SBIR → R&D;","indent_level":0}]},"history":[{"action":"created","actor_id":"system:import","timestamp":"2026-08-10T13:20:08.197Z","actor_name":"Document Import"}],"provenance":{"source":"imported","drafted_at":"2026-08-10T13:20:08.197Z","drafted_by":"system:import"},"library_eligible":true},{"id":"6423519b-1ea0-4f09-91c3-e57aa4a9c272","type":"text_block","style":{},"content":{"text":"pre-seed; goal: prove the market + sustained value to homebuilders."},"history":[{"action":"created","actor_id":"system:import","timestamp":"2026-08-10T13:20:08.197Z","actor_name":"Document Import"}],"provenance":{"source":"imported","drafted_at":"2026-08-10T13:20:08.197Z","drafted_by":"system:import"},"library_eligible":true},{"id":"4d6edbea-3bd1-4721-8e75-8627a11ec67c","type":"bulleted_list","style":{},"content":{"items":[{"text":"**Project plan (slides 17–18):** Hiring (Mo 1–2, $10k); R&D w/ **Converge** (Mo 3–4, $190k);","indent_level":0}]},"history":[{"action":"created","actor_id":"system:import","timestamp":"2026-08-10T13:20:08.197Z","actor_name":"Document Import"}],"provenance":{"source":"imported","drafted_at":"2026-08-10T13:20:08.197Z","drafted_by":"system:import"},"library_eligible":true},{"id":"711543d1-14a6-4e00-9319-d9dd8ea1b4b7","type":"text_block","style":{},"content":{"text":"Beta prototype (Mo 6–8); Grants+Funding (1–14 mo, $1.0M, TVSF/SBIR/VC); R&D on beta (1–12 mo, $450k); Tests & demos (9–14 mo, $30k); Final build (11–14 mo, $300k)."},"history":[{"action":"created","actor_id":"system:import","timestamp":"2026-08-10T13:20:08.197Z","actor_name":"Document Import"}],"provenance":{"source":"imported","drafted_at":"2026-08-10T13:20:08.197Z","drafted_by":"system:import"},"library_eligible":true},{"id":"17a92fbe-cee8-49a1-8b9f-318817fbf790","type":"bulleted_list","style":{},"content":{"items":[{"text":"**Budget (slides 19–20):** TVSF $200k — Personnel $40k, Equipment $120k, Supplies $10k,","indent_level":0}]},"history":[{"action":"created","actor_id":"system:import","timestamp":"2026-08-10T13:20:08.197Z","actor_name":"Document Import"}],"provenance":{"source":"imported","drafted_at":"2026-08-10T13:20:08.197Z","drafted_by":"system:import"},"library_eligible":true},{"id":"538c9c03-7172-48fa-a1ee-783694f7f17f","type":"text_block","style":{},"content":{"text":"Purchased Services $30k (Converge dev services + software partner; COTS + specialized parts; concrete supplies for prototype tests)."},"history":[{"action":"created","actor_id":"system:import","timestamp":"2026-08-10T13:20:08.197Z","actor_name":"Document Import"}],"provenance":{"source":"imported","drafted_at":"2026-08-10T13:20:08.197Z","drafted_by":"system:import"},"library_eligible":true},{"id":"bec21da0-d2d4-4664-8b27-ac7c7f97f58c","type":"heading","style":{},"content":{"text":"5. TVSF Proposal volume — drafted answers (7 pages; Abstract excluded)","level":2},"history":[{"action":"created","actor_id":"system:import","timestamp":"2026-08-10T13:20:08.197Z","actor_name":"Document Import"}],"provenance":{"source":"imported","drafted_at":"2026-08-10T13:20:08.197Z","drafted_by":"system:import"},"library_eligible":true},{"id":"dd76249b-524e-49b8-a33c-cb863d62bee7","type":"text_block","style":{},"content":{"text":"**Abstract (public, ¼ page).** Foundation is an Ohio pre-seed venture that 3D-prints the *formwork* for residential concrete foundations. By printing the foundation wall shape directly — with common, locally sourced concrete rather than proprietary mortar — Foundation eliminates the traditional build-strip-repair-clean formwork cycle, cutting foundation formwork labor from ~336 hours to ~25 and total formwork cost by roughly 47% on a typical 2,100 sq ft Ohio home. TVSF funds a beta prototype and third-party performance validation, de-risking a $23.7B U.S. formwork market and advancing Ohio''s housing-affordability and advanced-manufacturing agenda."},"history":[{"action":"created","actor_id":"system:import","timestamp":"2026-08-10T13:20:08.197Z","actor_name":"Document Import"}],"provenance":{"source":"imported","drafted_at":"2026-08-10T13:20:08.197Z","drafted_by":"system:import"},"library_eligible":true},{"id":"5b518f34-8dd7-4fd1-8cde-d68b3c84ec2d","type":"text_block","style":{},"content":{"text":"**#1 — Market Opportunity (TAM).** The 2026 U.S. housing market represents a **$410B TAM** against a structural **~500,000-home supply/demand gap**; \"locked-in\" 6% mortgages push builders toward new-build \"buy-down\" economics where every point of cost removed matters. Foundation targets the **formwork** line item of single-family new builds — a **$23.7B SAM** — with an initial serviceable-obtainable **$27.4M SOM** in its regional beachhead. Because foundation 3D printing lowers total home cost ~4% while removing the industry''s most labor-intensive, waste-prone step, it converts a cost center into a competitive advantage for builders operating on thin margins."},"history":[{"action":"created","actor_id":"system:import","timestamp":"2026-08-10T13:20:08.197Z","actor_name":"Document Import"}],"provenance":{"source":"imported","drafted_at":"2026-08-10T13:20:08.197Z","drafted_by":"system:import"},"library_eligible":true},{"id":"611b0021-93e0-4840-b717-0b89a41789b7","type":"text_block","style":{},"content":{"text":"**#2 — Overview of the Technology.** Foundation''s system prints a foundation''s wall geometry directly: a build plan is downloaded to the printer, concrete is pumped into the machine, and the nozzle lays concrete one layer at a time. A printing trolley moves laterally and vertically while the whole machine travels along runway rails; the system is electrically powered. Two differentiators define it: (a) it uses **common, locally sourced concrete**, not an expensive proprietary mortar; and (b) an **external gate controls material flow at the nozzle**, enabling clean starts/stops and consistent layers. The net effect eliminates the build-strip-repair-clean cycle, saving ~311 labor hours per home and cutting formwork production cost ~47–50% and material cost ~60–65% versus mortar-based concrete printers."},"history":[{"action":"created","actor_id":"system:import","timestamp":"2026-08-10T13:20:08.197Z","actor_name":"Document Import"}],"provenance":{"source":"imported","drafted_at":"2026-08-10T13:20:08.197Z","drafted_by":"system:import"},"library_eligible":true},{"id":"e49574e3-78c8-41d0-9ad9-33298086a1bf","type":"text_block","style":{},"content":{"text":"**#3 — Development Stage.** The technology is at **TRL 6–7**: core subsystems (delivery, nozzle gate, gantry motion) are demonstrated and the team is building a **beta prototype** for a relevant application environment. MVP customer requirements are explicit — rapid deployment, reduced labor, structural reliability, and use of locally sourced materials. TVSF''s role is to fund the beta prototype build and an independent third-party performance validation, moving the system from demonstrated subsystems (TRL 6–7) toward a field-validated first printer (TRL 7–8)."},"history":[{"action":"created","actor_id":"system:import","timestamp":"2026-08-10T13:20:08.197Z","actor_name":"Document Import"}],"provenance":{"source":"imported","drafted_at":"2026-08-10T13:20:08.197Z","drafted_by":"system:import"},"library_eligible":true},{"id":"0d5d243c-a858-4a7d-928f-3f4217b1ec26","type":"text_block","style":{},"content":{"text":"**#4 — Commercialization Strategy (SAM).** Entry is **proof-based**: local, fragmented buyers whose barriers are trust, portability, and cost, and whose workflow already relies on subcontractors. Foundation sells into that workflow as **\"printing as a service\"** to general contractors and developers, priced per cubic yard of concrete, and partners with **local schools and builders** for demos and workforce pipeline. The motion is **demos/tours → paid pilot → repeat jobs**, using non- dilutive **TVSF + SBIR Phase I** to reach a validated pilot before scaling into the $23.7B formwork SAM."},"history":[{"action":"created","actor_id":"system:import","timestamp":"2026-08-10T13:20:08.197Z","actor_name":"Document Import"}],"provenance":{"source":"imported","drafted_at":"2026-08-10T13:20:08.197Z","drafted_by":"system:import"},"library_eligible":true},{"id":"bec83a32-54ab-4b02-80bf-318a40a51365","type":"text_block","style":{},"content":{"text":"**#5 — Intellectual Property.** Foundation''s approach is anchored by two issued U.S. patents: **11,273,574** (\"Scalable Three-Dimensional Printing Apparatus\") covering the scalable gantry/print architecture, and **10,307,959 B2** (\"Concrete Delivery System\") covering the concrete delivery and nozzle-control mechanism. Together they protect the two core differentiators — the rail-scalable printer and the externally gated, local-concrete delivery path. Freedom-to-operate and continuation strategy around the nozzle-gate control are part of the funded work."},"history":[{"action":"created","actor_id":"system:import","timestamp":"2026-08-10T13:20:08.197Z","actor_name":"Document Import"}],"provenance":{"source":"imported","drafted_at":"2026-08-10T13:20:08.197Z","drafted_by":"system:import"},"library_eligible":true},{"id":"9868a304-952c-461d-b133-3428ffc12e20","type":"text_block","style":{},"content":{"text":"**#6 — Business Model & Pro-forma P&L (SOM / economic sense).** Foundation forms a **joint venture** per project, programs and prepares the print, and **charges per cubic yard of concrete placed**, at ≈$20,000 total price per job with a contribution margin of ≈**37.5%**. Printing-as-a-service keeps capital with Foundation and lowers the builder''s barrier to adoption. Against a $27.4M near-term SOM, a modest fleet of printers running repeat jobs reaches sustainable unit economics quickly; the pro-forma (in $1,000s) scales job volume as pilots convert to repeat contracts, with gross margin expanding as printer utilization rises."},"history":[{"action":"created","actor_id":"system:import","timestamp":"2026-08-10T13:20:08.197Z","actor_name":"Document Import"}],"provenance":{"source":"imported","drafted_at":"2026-08-10T13:20:08.197Z","drafted_by":"system:import"},"library_eligible":true},{"id":"dcd9bafa-ef2e-4e29-9f54-33c1799482c1","type":"text_block","style":{},"content":{"text":"**#7 — Current Financial Stage & Fundraising.** Foundation is **pre-seed**. The capital plan pairs **$200k TVSF** and **$150k SBIR Phase I** (non-dilutive, directed at R&D and the beta prototype) with a targeted **$1.8M+ equity** round. Equity investment is critical to scaling beyond the first printer; the non-dilutive grants exist to **prove the market and de-risk the technology first**, so the equity raise is priced on validated performance rather than on a concept. TVSF is the near-term unlock for the validated beta prototype that makes the round investable."},"history":[{"action":"created","actor_id":"system:import","timestamp":"2026-08-10T13:20:08.197Z","actor_name":"Document Import"}],"provenance":{"source":"imported","drafted_at":"2026-08-10T13:20:08.197Z","drafted_by":"system:import"},"library_eligible":true},{"id":"7aeedf04-dc18-4ae7-9382-90318d8db444","type":"text_block","style":{},"content":{"text":"**#8 — Team / Management.** **Kate Ulepic (CEO)** leads strategy and fundraising; **Conor Atkins (COO)** owns operations and print execution; **Connor Casey (CFO)** owns finance and the capital plan; **Will Curley (CTO)** owns the printer and delivery technology. The team has identified and is actively recruiting for its known gaps — legal advisor, fundraiser, technician, and homebuilder partner — and is mentored through the **Entrepreneurs'' Center** (Paul Jackson, VP Strategic Programs)."},"history":[{"action":"created","actor_id":"system:import","timestamp":"2026-08-10T13:20:08.197Z","actor_name":"Document Import"}],"provenance":{"source":"imported","drafted_at":"2026-08-10T13:20:08.197Z","drafted_by":"system:import"},"library_eligible":true},{"id":"52658812-49b6-431a-9f81-d242e7da1bed","type":"text_block","style":{},"content":{"text":"**#9 — Competitive Landscape.** Against **Traditional Formwork**, **Vitruvian**, and **COBOD International**, Foundation wins on the dimensions that decide adoption:"},"history":[{"action":"created","actor_id":"system:import","timestamp":"2026-08-10T13:20:08.197Z","actor_name":"Document Import"}],"provenance":{"source":"imported","drafted_at":"2026-08-10T13:20:08.197Z","drafted_by":"system:import"},"library_eligible":true},{"id":"74b7c9a4-8bd5-4dc6-8c2e-9f53f0a9fb4e","type":"text_block","style":{},"content":{"text":"| Dimension | Foundation | Traditional Formwork | Vitruvian | COBOD | |---|:--:|:--:|:--:|:--:| | Time (days) | ✓ | ✗ | ✓ | ✓ | | Deployment | ✓ | ✗ | ✓ | ✗ | | Material accessibility | ✓ | ✓ | ✗ | ✗ | | Project costs | ✓ | ✗ | ✗ | ✗ | | Scalability | ✓ | ✗ | ✓ | ✓ | | Repeatable workflow | ✓ | ✗ | ✓ | ✓ |"},"history":[{"action":"created","actor_id":"system:import","timestamp":"2026-08-10T13:20:08.197Z","actor_name":"Document Import"}],"provenance":{"source":"imported","drafted_at":"2026-08-10T13:20:08.197Z","drafted_by":"system:import"},"library_eligible":true},{"id":"63fc6a07-a439-4123-8701-1912bbffd783","type":"text_block","style":{},"content":{"text":"Foundation is the only option that combines **local-material accessibility** and **lowest project cost** with rapid, scalable, repeatable deployment — traditional formwork is slow and labor-heavy, while other printers depend on costly proprietary mortar."},"history":[{"action":"created","actor_id":"system:import","timestamp":"2026-08-10T13:20:08.197Z","actor_name":"Document Import"}],"provenance":{"source":"imported","drafted_at":"2026-08-10T13:20:08.197Z","drafted_by":"system:import"},"library_eligible":true},{"id":"31fe649a-34c1-4df8-aa52-23e6b8c675d1","type":"text_block","style":{},"content":{"text":"**#10 — Economic Impact (Ohio).** Foundation is Ohio-based and Ohio-building. It lowers the cost of new single-family homes in a state facing a supply gap, supports builder margins, and creates skilled advanced-manufacturing and print-operator jobs. By partnering with **local schools and builders** for demos and training, it seeds a regional workforce pipeline and keeps concrete spend with **local** suppliers rather than proprietary-mortar vendors — compounding the in-state economic return of each job."},"history":[{"action":"created","actor_id":"system:import","timestamp":"2026-08-10T13:20:08.197Z","actor_name":"Document Import"}],"provenance":{"source":"imported","drafted_at":"2026-08-10T13:20:08.197Z","drafted_by":"system:import"},"library_eligible":true},{"id":"8a8d3c60-c273-4189-b1e0-6e42a1af2598","type":"text_block","style":{},"content":{"text":"**#11 — Project Plan.** Milestones (name · description · success criteria · timeframe · approx. funds):"},"history":[{"action":"created","actor_id":"system:import","timestamp":"2026-08-10T13:20:08.197Z","actor_name":"Document Import"}],"provenance":{"source":"imported","drafted_at":"2026-08-10T13:20:08.197Z","drafted_by":"system:import"},"library_eligible":true},{"id":"06e45223-7107-4aa3-8b21-5cd95259c45d","type":"numbered_list","style":{},"content":{"items":[{"text":"**Hire core team** — fill technician/operator roles — team in place — Months 1–2 — **$10,000**.","indent_level":0},{"text":"**R&D with Converge** — engineer the beta printer + delivery/gate — validated subsystem specs —","indent_level":0}]},"history":[{"action":"created","actor_id":"system:import","timestamp":"2026-08-10T13:20:08.197Z","actor_name":"Document Import"}],"provenance":{"source":"imported","drafted_at":"2026-08-10T13:20:08.197Z","drafted_by":"system:import"},"library_eligible":true},{"id":"3fbe7ec9-bd77-482b-82eb-fcef637b8cb4","type":"text_block","style":{},"content":{"text":"Months 3–4 — **$190,000**."},"history":[{"action":"created","actor_id":"system:import","timestamp":"2026-08-10T13:20:08.197Z","actor_name":"Document Import"}],"provenance":{"source":"imported","drafted_at":"2026-08-10T13:20:08.197Z","drafted_by":"system:import"},"library_eligible":true},{"id":"b5bfab06-ab59-4f0b-8fd8-29ef51a29a98","type":"numbered_list","style":{},"content":{"items":[{"text":"**Beta prototype build** — assemble the first field-representative printer — prints a test wall to","indent_level":0}]},"history":[{"action":"created","actor_id":"system:import","timestamp":"2026-08-10T13:20:08.197Z","actor_name":"Document Import"}],"provenance":{"source":"imported","drafted_at":"2026-08-10T13:20:08.197Z","drafted_by":"system:import"},"library_eligible":true},{"id":"5b069e49-26b5-46c8-b0d2-a9072083fa84","type":"text_block","style":{},"content":{"text":"spec — Months 6–8 — (within R&D budget)."},"history":[{"action":"created","actor_id":"system:import","timestamp":"2026-08-10T13:20:08.197Z","actor_name":"Document Import"}],"provenance":{"source":"imported","drafted_at":"2026-08-10T13:20:08.197Z","drafted_by":"system:import"},"library_eligible":true},{"id":"ecb11c0b-ce70-409e-a96c-d53e70d18392","type":"numbered_list","style":{},"content":{"items":[{"text":"**Third-party performance validation** — independent structural + throughput test — passing","indent_level":0}]},"history":[{"action":"created","actor_id":"system:import","timestamp":"2026-08-10T13:20:08.197Z","actor_name":"Document Import"}],"provenance":{"source":"imported","drafted_at":"2026-08-10T13:20:08.197Z","drafted_by":"system:import"},"library_eligible":true},{"id":"8856e886-a057-46fb-a492-3d96a8c55d04","type":"text_block","style":{},"content":{"text":"validation report — Months 9–14 — **~$30,000**."},"history":[{"action":"created","actor_id":"system:import","timestamp":"2026-08-10T13:20:08.197Z","actor_name":"Document Import"}],"provenance":{"source":"imported","drafted_at":"2026-08-10T13:20:08.197Z","drafted_by":"system:import"},"library_eligible":true},{"id":"1013ecbd-23e6-4f8f-96aa-5c6a747f2ebb","type":"numbered_list","style":{},"content":{"items":[{"text":"**First printer build** — production-representative unit for pilots — pilot-ready printer —","indent_level":0}]},"history":[{"action":"created","actor_id":"system:import","timestamp":"2026-08-10T13:20:08.197Z","actor_name":"Document Import"}],"provenance":{"source":"imported","drafted_at":"2026-08-10T13:20:08.197Z","drafted_by":"system:import"},"library_eligible":true},{"id":"1ccada26-36a9-4bbb-9d7a-dea052701a3e","type":"text_block","style":{},"content":{"text":"Months 11–14 — **~$300,000 (blended grant/VC)**."},"history":[{"action":"created","actor_id":"system:import","timestamp":"2026-08-10T13:20:08.197Z","actor_name":"Document Import"}],"provenance":{"source":"imported","drafted_at":"2026-08-10T13:20:08.197Z","drafted_by":"system:import"},"library_eligible":true},{"id":"87bae4ed-f31c-42d6-968e-ddd4d16b7fc4","type":"heading","style":{},"content":{"text":"6. TVSF Budget volume — $200,000 (OTF Project Funds)","level":2},"history":[{"action":"created","actor_id":"system:import","timestamp":"2026-08-10T13:20:08.197Z","actor_name":"Document Import"}],"provenance":{"source":"imported","drafted_at":"2026-08-10T13:20:08.197Z","drafted_by":"system:import"},"library_eligible":true},{"id":"de77fc31-10e4-4224-95b7-619c04b907af","type":"text_block","style":{},"content":{"text":"| Spend type | OTF Project Funds | Notes | |---|--:|---| | Personnel | $40,000 | founding-team time + first technical hires against the beta build | | Equipment | $120,000 | COTS + specialized printer/delivery parts for the beta prototype | | Supplies | $10,000 | concrete + consumables to run prototype print tests | | Purchased Services | $30,000 | Converge development services + a software-development partner | | **Total** | **$200,000** | |"},"history":[{"action":"created","actor_id":"system:import","timestamp":"2026-08-10T13:20:08.197Z","actor_name":"Document Import"}],"provenance":{"source":"imported","drafted_at":"2026-08-10T13:20:08.197Z","drafted_by":"system:import"},"library_eligible":true},{"id":"293bdbd1-27f3-456f-b8fd-2f71b7ef3eb3","type":"text_block","style":{},"content":{"text":"Narrative: the bulk of the grant funds **Equipment** (COTS + specialized parts to build the beta prototype with Converge) and **Purchased Services** (Converge engineering + software partner); **Supplies** cover concrete for prototype testing; **Personnel** covers founding-team time and the first technical hire."},"history":[{"action":"created","actor_id":"system:import","timestamp":"2026-08-10T13:20:08.197Z","actor_name":"Document Import"}],"provenance":{"source":"imported","drafted_at":"2026-08-10T13:20:08.197Z","drafted_by":"system:import"},"library_eligible":true},{"id":"2c068f9a-ceab-4e46-bda1-0b0c335e0a05","type":"heading","style":{},"content":{"text":"7. Foundation spotlight buckets (interest areas → for ranking opportunities)","level":2},"history":[{"action":"created","actor_id":"system:import","timestamp":"2026-08-10T13:20:08.197Z","actor_name":"Document Import"}],"provenance":{"source":"imported","drafted_at":"2026-08-10T13:20:08.197Z","drafted_by":"system:import"},"library_eligible":true},{"id":"9197beb9-0cb7-49e5-becf-2695e6040907","type":"numbered_list","style":{},"content":{"items":[{"text":"**Additive Construction & 3D Printing** (primary)","indent_level":0},{"text":"**Advanced Manufacturing / Automation**","indent_level":0},{"text":"**Construction Technology & Housing Affordability**","indent_level":0},{"text":"**Materials — Concrete & Low-Carbon Cement**","indent_level":0},{"text":"**Non-dilutive Capital (SBIR/STTR + State)**","indent_level":0}]},"history":[{"action":"created","actor_id":"system:import","timestamp":"2026-08-10T13:20:08.197Z","actor_name":